{
  "_readme": "Language-neutral exhibition data: official titles, sizes, years, images and where each work hangs. All visitor-facing texts are in src/i18n/en.json and hu.json. Videos: 'video.loop' is the short silent loop played on the screen in 3D (public/video, cut from the artist's files); 'video.full' are the full videos, played in the artwork viewer only after their button is pressed: 'youtube' is the YouTube video id (played from youtube-nocookie.com) and wins over 'drive', the Google Drive file id, so moving a video to YouTube is one line, \"youtube\": \"<id>\", in its entry. An entry's 'title' names a full video whose title is not the work's (Siluett, the projection of Let it Flow); 'label' is the button's text in 'ui.viewer' of the i18n files. 'desc' names the artist's text in 'descriptions' in the i18n files; 'situ' lists a work's installation photos. 'photo' names the installation photograph that shows the work in place (the photographer's file name; the photographs are not in this repository); for a work without a 'situ' list, its in-situ view (the image's '-situ' file) was cut from it. Where the images a work shows were cut from other photographs, 'imageSources' names the file each image comes from, as in scripts/crops.json (\"repro\"); there 'photo' is a reference only and no image on the site is cut from it. 'contacts' fills the Contact panel: an entry with an empty 'href' stays hidden until it is filled in. 'monitor' is the photographed frame (with its rods) drawn around a screen; its opening is the screen. 'video.viewer' is played in the artwork viewer instead of the loop. 'rights' is the work's rights statement ('uri', from rightsstatements.org) and its credit line, both from the Google Sheet 'works' (rights_statement, rights_holder): it covers the work only; the installation photographs and the documentation videos are credited apart (© Kristóf Szabó, see NOTICE). 'reconstruction' says how the work was reconstructed, from the paradata (src/data/paradata.json, a copy of the Google Sheet 'paradata', tab paradata_3): 'aspects' lists every paradata row that names the work, with the row's id, element and status as the Sheet gives them (measured, inferred, invented, not recorded); 'status' is filled in only when all the aspects have the same status, otherwise it is empty and 'note' says which aspects have which status. scripts/paradata-import.mjs writes 'reconstruction'; nothing in it is filled in by hand.",
